\begin_layout Standard
As I stated previously, I tested the hypothesis 
\begin_inset Formula $H_{0}:\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}$
\end_inset

 in the function that runs the FE regression.
 The code for this test and these regressions can be found at the end of
 the assignment.
 Important to note, 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha=.05$
\end_inset

.
 After the test, I obtained 
\begin_inset Formula $t=-1.3908$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $P=0.1673$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, we fail to reject the null hypothesis.
 Instead, we can estimate a more parsimonious model.
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
\log(\mbox{\emph{crime}}_{it}) & = & \theta_{0}+\theta_{1}d78_{t}+\beta_{1}\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-1}+\beta_{2}\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-2}+c_{i}+u_{it}\\
 & = & \theta_{0}+\theta_{1}d78_{t}+\beta_{1}\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-1}+\beta_{1}\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-2}+c_{i}+u_{it}\\
\log(\mbox{\emph{crime}}_{it}) & = & \theta_{0}+\theta_{1}d78_{t}+\beta_{1}(\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-1}+\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-2})+c_{i}+u_{it}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

I downloaded the data in NORWAY into STATA, and then I exported the data
 for 
\emph on

\begin_inset Formula $\log(\mbox{\emph{crime}}_{it})$
\end_inset

, 
\emph default

\begin_inset Formula $d78_{t}$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-1}$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-2}$
\end_inset

, into a csv file.
 Within the csv file, I then added the variables 
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-1}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-2}$
\end_inset

 together to form a new variable, 
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-1}+\mbox{\emph{clrprc}}_{i,t-2}$
\end_inset

.
 I used MATLAB to run a FE , and I calculated heteroskedasticity-robust
 standard errors for the FE estimates.
 Important to note, the t-test coded in the FE function was commented out,
 so the regression would run.
 The code for this regression can be found at the end of the assignment.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha=0.5$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

